keywords:
  - galaxy rotation curves
  - SPARC
  - dark matter
  - information geometry
  - neural cosmology
abstract: >-
  Three information-geometric models of galactic rotation compared on the
  171-galaxy SPARC sample: unconstrained pointer, constrained pointer (physical
  prior on halo extent) and an NFW baseline. The constrained pointer wins AIC on
  60 of 171 galaxies; halo extent correlates with inferred information mass
  (rho = +0.19, q_FDR = 0.04); 4 of 6 residual-structure features correlate with
  galactic age. Code, data and fit diagnostics included.
